SUBJECT (quoted and summarised from the dataset's own subjects.xlsx, samples.xlsx and README.md)
  `sub-SC001`: Homo sapiens, male, 41 years, EMBALMED CADAVER. Both sciatic nerves. Six samples, each a
  segment of sciatic nerve about 9 cm long: SCL2 / SCL3 / SCL4 (left) and SCR2 / SCR3 / SCR4 (right), the
  larger sample number more distal. Preparation: cadaver embalming (protocols.io 10.17504/protocols.io.kxygx4wm4l8j/v1),
  phosphotungstic-acid (PTA) staining (10.17504/protocols.io.5qpvod95xg4o/v1), microCT of the excised segments
  (10.17504/protocols.io.36wgqpd55vk5/v1) at 11.4 um isotropic resolution, segmentation with nnU-Net v2.
  Funding named by the dataset: NIH SPARC OT2OD025349 and 75N98022C00018, VA 1I21RX005151,
  AFOSR FA9550-23-F-0014.

